From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Arun Iyengar <aiyengar1990@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 22:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] configs: orangepi_zero2: keep the environment in
 /boot/uboot.env

Armbian images have a single ext4 partition, so the default FAT
environment cannot be used. Keep it in /boot/uboot.env on mmc 0:1.
U-Boot cannot write ext4 with metadata_csum (the mke2fs default), so
saveenv fails there.

Signed-off-by: Arun Iyengar <aiyengar1990@gmail.com>
---
 configs/orangepi_zero2_defconfig | 5 +++++
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+)

diff --git a/configs/orangepi_zero2_defconfig b/configs/orangepi_zero2_defconfig
index a45402e5ba8..658d2510bb0 100644
--- a/configs/orangepi_zero2_defconfig
+++ b/configs/orangepi_zero2_defconfig
@@ -14,6 +14,11 @@ CONFIG_SPL_SUNXI_LED_STATUS=y
 CONFIG_SPL_SUNXI_LED_STATUS_GPIO=76
 # CONFIG_SYS_MALLOC_CLEAR_ON_INIT is not set
 CONFIG_SPL_I2C=y
+# CONFIG_ENV_IS_IN_FAT is not set
+CONFIG_ENV_IS_IN_EXT4=y
+CONFIG_ENV_EXT4_INTERFACE="mmc"
+CONFIG_ENV_EXT4_DEVICE_AND_PART="0:1"
+CONFIG_ENV_EXT4_FILE="/boot/uboot.env"
 CONFIG_SYS_I2C_SUN8I_RSB=y
 CONFIG_MTD=y
 CONFIG_SPI_FLASH_MACRONIX=y
-- 
Armbian

